{color.GG}dynav_ignore.lst {color.N}is the exclusion list used by dynav during startup.
It prevents selected first-level directories under {color.GG}$__aresroot__ {color.N}from being exported as environment variables.

Example {color.BB}dynav_ignore.lst{color.N}:
{color.DG}# comment{color.N}
myd1folder
something

Example:
    {color.GG}$__aresroot__/bin          {color.N}-> {color.YY}$__bin__{color.N}
    {color.GG}$__aresroot__/myd1folder   {color.N}-> not exported
    {color.GG}$__aresroot__/something    {color.N}-> not exported
    {color.GG}$__aresroot__/test         {color.N}-> {color.YY}$__test__{color.N}
    {color.GG}$__aresroot__/module       {color.N}-> {color.YY}$__module__{color.N}

{color.YY}Note{color.N}:
    {color.R}- {color.N}dynav reads this file once during startup.
    {color.R}- {color.N}Only first-level directories under {color.GG}$__aresroot__ {color.N}are checked.